# RiskSentinel AI v2.0 — Production-Grade Architecture Overhaul

Transform the functional prototype into a hackathon-winning, production-grade AI Risk Management platform with multi-model ML, agentic LLM intelligence, and a modern command-center frontend.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **LLM Provider Choice**: The Agentic Risk Investigator needs an LLM API. The plan defaults to **Google Gemini** (free tier available, `google-generativeai` SDK). If you prefer OpenAI, Anthropic, or a local model (Ollama), let me know — it only affects `backend/services/llm_agent.py`.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Redis vs In-Memory Cache**: For hackathon scope, I'm using **`cachetools` (TTL in-memory cache)** instead of Redis. This gives us sub-millisecond cache hits with zero infrastructure overhead. Redis can be swapped in later with a single service change. Acceptable?

> [!WARNING]
> **Dataset Observation**: The current dataset has 5 merchant categories (`travel`, `fashion`, `electronics`, `grocery`, `gaming`) and 10 countries (`FR`, `US`, `TR`, `PL`, `ES`, `IT`, `RO`, `GB`, `NL`, `DE`). The existing `app.py` only handles 3 merchant categories and 3 countries in its feature engineering — the new system will handle all values dynamically.

