## Proposed Changes

### Component 1 — ML Pipeline Overhaul

#### [NEW] [`backend/ml/preprocess.py`](file:///d:/Coding/Machine%20Learning/razorpay-risk-sentinel/backend/ml/preprocess.py)

Enhanced preprocessing that **persists the fitted `ColumnTransformer`** to `preprocessor.pkl` so the API can apply identical transformations at inference time. Key changes:
- Saves `preprocessor.pkl` alongside the data — eliminates the current bug where `app.py` does manual (inconsistent) feature engineering
- Saves `feature_names.json` mapping for SHAP interpretability
- Handles all 5 merchant categories and 10 countries from the dataset (not just 3)
- Same stratified 80/20 split with `random_state=42` — zero leakage

#### [NEW] [`backend/ml/train_xgboost.py`](file:///d:/Coding/Machine%20Learning/razorpay-risk-sentinel/backend/ml/train_xgboost.py)

Replaces the Decision Tree with **XGBoost** (`XGBClassifier`):
- `scale_pos_weight` calculated from class imbalance ratio (~13.3:1) for proper fraud recall
- `max_depth=6`, `n_estimators=200`, `learning_rate=0.1`, `eval_metric='aucpr'`
- Saves to `artifacts/xgboost_model.pkl`
- Generates and saves a SHAP `TreeExplainer` to `artifacts/shap_explainer.pkl`

**Why XGBoost over Deep Learning**: For 300K tabular rows with 17 features, XGBoost consistently outperforms neural networks on fraud detection benchmarks. It's also natively explainable via SHAP TreeExplainer (exact, not approximate). This is the right call for hackathon judging — "we chose the empirically best model" > "we used deep learning because it sounds cool."

#### [NEW] [`backend/ml/train_anomaly.py`](file:///d:/Coding/Machine%20Learning/razorpay-risk-sentinel/backend/ml/train_anomaly.py)

Adds an **Isolation Forest** unsupervised anomaly detector:
- Trained on **non-fraud transactions only** from the training set (learns "normal" behavior)
- `contamination=0.02` (matching the ~2.2% fraud rate)
- At inference, outputs an anomaly score [-1, 1] that acts as a **second opinion** alongside XGBoost
- Catches zero-day fraud patterns the supervised model hasn't seen

#### [NEW] [`backend/ml/evaluate.py`](file:///d:/Coding/Machine%20Learning/razorpay-risk-sentinel/backend/ml/evaluate.py)

Unified evaluation script:
- Classification metrics: Precision, Recall, F1, AUC-PR, AUC-ROC
- Confusion matrix with financial impact (₹1,500 FP cost, ₹4,000 FN loss)
- SHAP summary plot saved as image for the dashboard
- Comparison output: Decision Tree vs XGBoost performance

